{
  "summary": "The current UI implementation does not fully satisfy the DESIGN.md specification. The most critical problem is that the sign‑up flow breaks because the required \"Confirm password\" field is missing, preventing users from completing registration. In addition, primary navigation is not consistently displayed on authenticated screens, which can leave users stranded. Several components also violate the design‑token system, lack required interaction states (focus rings, loading indicators), and miss accessibility details such as aria‑labels, autocomplete attributes, and proper error handling. Below is a prioritized list of concrete issues and the fixes needed to bring the product up to spec.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/Register.tsx",
      "issue": "The sign‑up form does not render a \"Confirm password\" input. The automated primary‑flow test times out when trying to fill this field, and the UI cannot validate that the two passwords match.",
      "fix": "Add a confirm‑password <input> with a visible <label> placed above the field. Use autocomplete=\"new-password\", set type=\"password\", and implement client‑side validation that compares it to the original password. Show an inline error (e.g., \"Passwords do not match.\") and link the error message via aria-describedby. Include the field in the payload sent to /auth/register."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "frontend/src/App.tsx (or the top‑level routing/layout component)",
      "issue": "Primary navigation (BottomNav on mobile, HeaderNav on desktop) is not rendered on every signed‑in screen, violating the requirement that navigation must always be visible.",
      "fix": "Create a Layout component that includes <HeaderNav/> for viewport ≥1280 px and <BottomNav/> for smaller viewports. Wrap all authenticated routes (Dashboard, Receipts, Mileage, Export) with this Layout so the navigation bar is present on every page."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/Register.tsx",
      "issue": "The \"Create account\" button is disabled silently when validation errors exist, instead of remaining enabled and showing a loading spinner after submission. This departs from the sign‑up best‑practice described in the spec.",
      "fix": "Keep the button enabled as long as the form fields are valid. When the user taps it, replace the label with a spinner (using the LoadingSpinner component) and disable further interaction until the request resolves."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/Button.tsx (and any component‑specific CSS files)",
      "issue": "Hard‑coded color values (e.g., background:#0066FF) and size values are used instead of the design tokens defined in src/index.css (var(--c-primary), var(--size‑16), var(--radius‑8), etc.).",
      "fix": "Replace all literal colors, font‑sizes, spacings, and radii with the corresponding CSS variables. Update the component styles to reference the token palette (e.g., background: var(--c-primary); font-size: var(--size-16); border-radius: var(--radius-8);)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/* (all interactive elements)",
      "issue": "Interactive elements lack a visible focus indicator. Some components set \"outline: none\" or do not inherit the global \":focus-visible\" rule, making keyboard navigation difficult.",
      "fix": "Remove any custom outline overrides. Ensure that every focusable element shows the global focus ring defined by :focus-visible { outline: var(--focus-ring); outline-offset: 2px; } or explicitly add that rule to the component’s :focus-visible state."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/* (icon‑only buttons such as delete, FAB, etc.)",
      "issue": "Icon‑only buttons do not provide an accessible name (aria‑label) and decorative icons are not marked aria‑hidden, causing screen‑reader users to miss their purpose.",
      "fix": "Add descriptive aria-label attributes to all icon‑only buttons (e.g., <button aria-label=\"Delete receipt\">) and set aria-hidden=\"true\" on purely decorative SVG icons."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/* (form inputs in Login, Register, ReceiptUpload, MileageForm)",
      "issue": "Form controls lack appropriate autocomplete attributes and do not set aria‑invalid or aria‑describedby when validation fails.",
      "fix": "Add autocomplete=\"email\" to email fields, autocomplete=\"current-password\" to login password fields, autocomplete=\"new-password\" to registration password fields, and autocomplete=\"off\" for numeric fields where needed. When a field is invalid, set aria-invalid=\"true\" and link the error message via aria-describedby."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/ReceiptUpload.tsx",
      "issue": "The file picker does not display the required copy about supported formats or maximum file size, and the <input type=\"file\"> lacks an \"accept\" attribute to restrict file types.",
      "fix": "Add a descriptive text element (e.g., <p class=\"help-text\">Supported formats: JPG, PNG, PDF. Max size 5 MB.</p>) near the picker and set accept=\"image/jpeg,image/png,application/pdf\" on the input element."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/PasswordField.tsx (or Register.tsx if password field is inline)",
      "issue": "Password inputs do not include a show/hide toggle, which reduces usability for users with visual impairments.",
      "fix": "Add a button inside the password field that toggles the input type between \"password\" and \"text\". Provide an aria-label that switches between \"Show password\" and \"Hide password\"."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/Toast.tsx",
      "issue": "Toast notifications are not marked with role=\"status\" (or role=\"alert\" for error toasts) and lack aria‑live attributes, so screen readers may not announce them.",
      "fix": "Wrap toast content in an element with role=\"status\" and aria-live=\"polite\" for success/info toasts, and role=\"alert\" with aria-live=\"assertive\" for error toasts."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/ExportButtons.tsx",
      "issue": "Export PDF/CSV buttons are missing tooltips that explain the action, which are required by the copy spec.",
      "fix": "Add a title attribute or a custom tooltip component with the text from the spec (e.g., title=\"Download a PDF ready for tax filing\")."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/OfflineBanner.tsx (not currently present)",
      "issue": "The UI does not display an offline banner when the network is unavailable, contrary to the design spec.",
      "fix": "Implement a component that listens for the \"online\" and \"offline\" events and renders a banner using the '--c-offline-bg' background token with the copy \"You’re offline – data will sync when you’re back online.\"."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/Modal.tsx (if modal component exists)",
      "issue": "Modal dialogs (e.g., delete confirmation) do not enforce focus trapping or return focus to the opener on close, which can break keyboard navigation.",
      "fix": "Use a focus‑trap library or implement manual focus management: on open, move focus to the first focusable element; on close, return focus to the element that triggered the modal. Ensure the modal has role=\"dialog\" with aria-modal=\"true\"."
    }
  ]
}

