{
  "summary": "Overall the UI is clean, passes axe and Lighthouse, and most visual elements render correctly. However, the core user‑journey is broken: the sign‑up flow does not auto‑login, causing a 401 on the dashboard and preventing the empty‑state message defined in the design spec from ever appearing. This is a high‑severity blocker. In addition there are several medium‑severity gaps – missing ARIA labels on icon‑only FAB actions, inconsistent use of the design‑token CSS variables, and minor mismatches in error‑state copy and navigation presence. Low‑severity issues include missing password‑rule hints and offline‑banner implementation.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "backend/app/routers/auth.py",
      "issue": "The `/auth/register` endpoint only returns the newly created user (id, email) and never issues a JWT. The spec requires auto‑login after sign‑up, but the client receives no token, so subsequent authenticated calls (e.g., `/dashboard/summary`) return 401 and the dashboard never reaches the empty state.",
      "fix": "Modify the register handler to create an access token (reuse `auth.create_access_token`) and return it in the same shape as the login endpoint (`{ access_token: ..., token_type: \"bearer\" }`). Update the OpenAPI schema accordingly."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/Register.tsx",
      "issue": "The Register component does not store a JWT after sign‑up (because the backend does not return one) and does not navigate to the Dashboard. This leaves the UI in an unauthenticated state and causes the flow test to timeout at step 7.",
      "fix": "After adjusting the backend to return a token, update the Register component to save the token (e.g., in localStorage or a React context) and programmatically navigate to the Dashboard on successful response."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/Dashboard.tsx",
      "issue": "When the summary API returns an error (e.g., 401), the UI shows a generic error banner or blank screen instead of the spec‑defined message \"Failed to load data. Retry.\" and does not provide a retry button.",
      "fix": "Add error handling that matches the design spec: display a banner with the exact copy, include a retry button that re‑calls the summary endpoint, and ensure the banner uses the `--c-error-bg` token and focus‑visible styling."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/Layout.tsx",
      "issue": "The floating action button (FAB) is rendered as an icon‑only button without a descriptive `aria-label`. Screen readers will not announce its purpose (Add Receipt / Add Mileage).",
      "fix": "Add `aria-label` props to the FAB based on its context (e.g., `aria-label=\"Add receipt\"` or `aria-label=\"Add mileage\"`). Ensure the button also has `role=\"button\"` and is focusable."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "frontend/src/index.css",
      "issue": "Design tokens (`var(--c-primary)`, `var(--space-8)`, etc.) are defined in `src/index.css` but the component styles use hard‑coded colors and spacing (e.g., `background:#0066FF`, `margin:16px`) instead of the CSS variables, violating the token‑usage rule.",
      "fix": "Refactor component CSS (or CSS‑in‑JS) to reference the defined CSS variables for colors, spacing, radii, and focus rings. For example, replace `background:#0066FF` with `background:var(--c-primary)`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/ExportButtons.tsx",
      "issue": "Export screen displays two large buttons but lacks the secondary button styling (transparent background with primary border) described in the design spec, and the focus ring is not applied on keyboard navigation.",
      "fix": "Implement the secondary button variant using the token‑based styles (`background:transparent; border:1px solid var(--c-primary); color:var(--c-primary)`) and ensure `:focus-visible` applies `outline: var(--focus-ring);`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/ReceiptUpload.tsx",
      "issue": "The file input description (“Supported formats: JPG, PNG, PDF. Max size 5 MB.”) and the help text for the date picker are missing, diverging from the copy spec. Also the error banner for server‑side upload failures does not match the required copy.",
      "fix": "Add a `<p class=\"help-text\">Supported formats: …</p>` below the file picker and ensure all error banners use the exact copy from the spec (e.g., \"Upload failed. Please try again.\")."
    },
    {
