{
  "summary": "The UI base is solid with high Lighthouse scores, design tokens applied, and no axe violations, but the primary sign‑up flow crashes due to missing auth handling and a handful of missing spec‑level details. The dashboard never renders its empty state because the JWT token isn’t attached to the request after auto‑login, causing a 401 and breaking the user journey (high severity). Secondary issues include missing copy for several error/empty states, incomplete accessibility markup, and a few UI interactions that don’t fully match the design spec (medium/low severity).",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/Layout.tsx",
      "issue": "After sign‑up the app does not store the returned JWT or send it with the dashboard request, so /dashboard/summary returns 401. The empty‑state copy \"No data yet. Add a receipt or mileage to get started.\" never appears, breaking step 7 of the primary flow.",
      "fix": "Persist the access_token (e.g., in localStorage or HttpOnly cookie) and configure the Axios instance to include `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on every request. After registration automatically set the auth header and trigger a dashboard reload."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/Register.tsx",
      "issue": "Form fields lack visible `<label>` elements (MUI TextField uses placeholder only) and autocomplete attributes, and there is no password‑rule helper or show/hide toggle. Inline validation errors are displayed but not linked via `aria-describedby`.",
      "fix": "Wrap each TextField with a `<label>` element (or use MUI’s `label` prop that renders a visible label), add `autoComplete` props (`email`, `new-password`), include a password‑rules hint, add a show/hide eye icon button with an accessible `aria-label`, and associate error messages via `aria-describedby` and `aria-invalid=\"true\"`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/Login.tsx",
      "issue": "Login form also uses placeholders without visible labels, missing autocomplete (`email`, `current-password`), and the submit button becomes disabled instead of showing a loading spinner. This violates the no‑silently‑disabled‑submit rule.",
      "fix": "Add visible `<label>` elements, set appropriate `autoComplete` attributes, replace disabled state with a loading spinner inside the button while preserving its size, and ensure the button remains focusable."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/ReceiptUpload.tsx",
      "issue": "Receipt upload form does not show the required field‑level hints (e.g., \"Supported formats: JPG, PNG, PDF. Max size 5 MB.\") and the permission‑denied dialog is not wired to the native permission API, so the UI never displays the \"Open settings?\" flow.",
      "fix": "Add a helper text component below the file input with the copy from the spec, detect `PermissionDeniedError` on mobile, and render a modal with the exact message and two buttons labeled \"Cancel\" and \"Open Settings\"."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/ExportButtons.tsx",
      "issue": "Export buttons lack tooltips matching the spec and the loading state replaces the label with a spinner but does not disable the sibling button, allowing double clicks.",
      "fix": "Add `title` attributes (or MUI Tooltip) with the specified copy, disable both export buttons while one is loading, and show the spinner in place of the label."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/Dashboard.tsx",
      "issue": "The offline banner uses default MUI colors instead of the `--c-offline-bg` token, and the banner text does not match the exact spec copy (capitalization differs).",
      "fix": "Apply `style={{ backgroundColor: 'var(--c-offline-bg)' }}` and update the text to \"You’re offline – data will sync when you’re back online.\""
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/Layout.tsx",
      "issue": "Bottom navigation icons have a visual hit‑area of 40 × 40 px, which is below the required 44 × 44 px touch target.",
      "fix": "Increase the button’s padding or add an invisible `::before` hit‑area to meet the 44 px minimum."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "frontend/dist/assets/index-GNEO6xVf.css",
      "issue": "Custom class names like `.fab` and `.card` exist but there are no corresponding BEM‑style component CSS files; they rely on global CSS which could lead to style leakage.",
      "fix": "Modularise styles (e.g., CSS modules or styled‑components) and ensure each component only imports its own token‑based stylesheet."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/Dashboard.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing ARIA live region for the summary loading spinner (`aria-live=\"polite\"`), which is required for screen‑reader users to hear \"Loading summary…\".",
      "fix": "Wrap the spinner in a `<div role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">Loading summary…</div>`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/MileageForm.tsx",
      "issue": "Date picker does not include a visible instruction \"Select the date the receipt was issued\" (copy mismatch) and lacks `aria-describedby` linking to that help text.",
      "fix": "Add a help text component below the date picker with the specified copy and reference it via `aria-describedby` on the input."
    }
  ]
}

